 "intro": "Herdonia in Apulia, 210 BC. The town, which went over to Hannibal, is ready to return to Rome. You are the proconsul Gnaeus Fulvius Centumalus, camped nearby with two legions.",
 "debrief": "In Livy’s account, Fulvius camped carelessly near Herdonia. Hannibal marched quickly and offered battle; Fulvius drew up in a long, thin line, and Hannibal’s hidden cavalry fell on his camp and rear. Fulvius and eleven military tribunes were killed, and Livy gives Roman losses as between 7,000 and 13,000. Hannibal burned Herdonia and moved its people. It was one of two Roman defeats at Herdonia, the other in 212 BC. The other choices are what-ifs.",
